{"name":"Wine Tasting","hex":"#492a34","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"},{"term":"tasting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small amount of food or drink.","The taking of a small amount of food or drink into the mouth in order to taste it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of taste"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tasting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wine tasting","blocks":[{"text":"Wine tasting is the sensory examination and evaluation of wine. While the practice of wine tasting is as ancient as its production, a more formalized methodology has slowly become established from the 14th century onward. Modern, professional wine tasters use a constantly evolving specialized terminology which is used to describe the range of perceived flavors, aromas and general characteristics of a wine. More informal, recreational tasting may use similar terminology, usually involving a much less analytical process for a more general, personal appreciation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Monk_Testing_Wine_-_Antonio_Casanova_y_Estorach.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Monk_Testing_Wine_-_Antonio_Casanova_y_Estorach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_tasting","wikidata":"Q2166448"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Degustation","blocks":[{"text":"Dégustation is the careful, appreciative tasting of various food, focusing on the gustatory system, the senses, and high culinary art. Dégustation is more likely to involve sampling small portions of all of a chef's signature dishes in one sitting. Usually consisting of many courses, it may be accompanied by a matching wine degustation which complements each dish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/D%C3%A9gustation_automnale.jpg/330px-D%C3%A9gustation_automnale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Degustation","wikidata":"Q1932115"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Porto.Grahams02.jpg/500px-Porto.Grahams02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Porto.Grahams02.jpg/500px-Porto.Grahams02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ready tasting room of port wine in a wine cellar of a producer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APorto.Grahams02.jpg"},{"s